## File Ownership and Conflict Policy

Before dispatching parallel workstreams, assign file ownership.

Rules:
- Two write workstreams must not edit the same file by default.
- If overlap is likely, serialize or make one workstream read-only.
- Shared config/schema/API files create a contract boundary; route or serialize.
- Docs-only streams can run beside code streams if files do not overlap.
- Read-only review, audit, and test-planning streams can run in parallel freely.
- Heavy builds/tests should be sequenced unless cheap and isolated.
- Re-check git status before and after integrating each workstream.
- Never stage unrelated/generated files.

Conflict template:

```text
