# Hermes Kanban CLI Command Reference

Use these general-purpose commands when the active workflow authorizes the Hermes CLI. Replace uppercase placeholders. Current V direction, ticket comments, review ownership, and project safety rules may narrow this surface.

## Core heartbeat commands

### 1. Discover work

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG list --mine --json
```

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG list --status ready --json
```

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG list --status running --json
```

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG list --status blocked --json
```

### 2. Read the complete task

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG show TASK_ID --json
```

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG context TASK_ID
```

Codex should run both before its first edit and rerun `show` before major transitions or final handoff.

### 3. Claim a task

Only manually launched workers need this. Dispatcher workers are already claimed.

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG claim TASK_ID --ttl 900
```

### 3a. Return a blocked card to In Progress

Heartbeat-protocol grants one narrow autonomous status transition: the current assigned `[Codex]` card may move from `Blocked` to `In Progress` (native status `running`) so the same worker can perform Hermes-requested rework.

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG unblock TASK_ID --reason "Returning the same blocked Codex card to In Progress for Hermes-requested rework"
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG claim TASK_ID --ttl 900
```

Use these commands only for the same blocked card. Do not use this exception to change any other status, route a successor, create a duplicate writer, or mark Done. Hermes alone owns Done.

If `block_loop_detected` has already relabeled the same blocked card as `triage`, `unblock` will refuse it. Recover only that exact card through the minimum native path:

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG promote TASK_ID "Recovering this same auto-triaged blocked card to In Progress for rework" --json
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG claim TASK_ID --ttl 900
```

This exception is not permission to promote ordinary triage work, change another card, route a successor, or mark Done.

### 4. Post a worker claim

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG comment --author Codex TASK_ID "WORKER CLAIM: task accepted; scope and latest comments read; beginning preflight."
```

### 5. Post progress comments

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG comment --author Codex TASK_ID "CODEX HEARTBEAT: PHASE; evidence: EVIDENCE; next action: NEXT_ACTION."
```

### 6. Emit a liveness heartbeat

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG heartbeat TASK_ID --note "CURRENT_PHASE"
```

Examples:

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG heartbeat TASK_ID --note "Reproduced RED; implementing minimum correction"
```

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG heartbeat TASK_ID --note "Running focused regression tests"
```

### 7. Inspect attempts and logs

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG runs TASK_ID --json
```

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG log TASK_ID --tail 20000
```

### 8. Inspect diagnostics and board state

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG diagnostics --task TASK_ID --json
```

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG diagnostics --severity error --task TASK_ID --json
```

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG stats --json
```

### 9. Follow task events

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG tail TASK_ID --interval 5
```

Codex should not post duplicate comments while nothing changes.

### 10. Post a review handoff

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG comment --author Codex TASK_ID "READY FOR REVIEW: files changed: FILES; tests: TEST_RESULTS; residual risks: RISKS; exact next action: REVIEW."
```

### 11. Block on an unfinished dependency

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG block --kind dependency TASK_ID "Blocked on dependency DEPENDENCY_ID: REASON"
```

### 12. Block for human input

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG block --kind needs_input TASK_ID "Human decision required: EXACT_DECISION"
```

### 13. Block on missing capability

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG block --kind capability TASK_ID "Required capability unavailable: EXACT_CAPABILITY"
```

### 14. Block on a transient failure

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG block --kind transient TASK_ID "Transient failure after retries: EXACT_FAILURE"
```

### 15. Complete a task â€” Hermes only

This command is documented for the Hermes/reviewer surface. Codex heartbeat workers must never call it because Hermes alone owns Done:

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG complete TASK_ID --summary "Completed TASK_OUTCOME" --metadata '{"changed_files":["PATH"],"tests_run":["COMMAND"],"findings":[],"residual_risks":[]}'
```

Codex always posts `READY FOR REVIEW` instead of calling `complete`.

